# UI conventions

- Styling: **Tailwind CSS v4** via `@tailwindcss/vite` and `src/styles.css`.
- Components: **shadcn/ui** under `src/components/ui/`. Prefer existing primitives
  (`Button`, `Input`, etc.) before adding new ones.
- Add or update shadcn components with the latest CLI — do not copy outdated
  snippets by hand:

```bash
pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add button
```

- Use `cn()` from `src/lib/utils.ts` for class merging.
- App shell lives in `Header` / `Footer` / theme toggle — rebrand there rather
  than introducing a parallel layout system.
- Keep demo-only UI under `src/routes/demo/**` or clearly named `demo.*` files.

## Color tokens (shadcn only)

- Colors come **only** from the shadcn token set defined in `src/styles.css`
  (`:root` / `.dark`): `background`, `foreground`, `card`, `popover`, `primary`,
  `secondary`, `muted`, `accent`, `destructive`, `border`, `input`, `ring`,
  `chart-*`, `sidebar-*`, and `radius`.
- Style with the Tailwind utilities those tokens back — e.g. `bg-primary`,
  `text-muted-foreground`, `border`, `bg-card`, `ring-ring`.
- Do **not** introduce a parallel palette: no custom `--brand-*` / theme CSS
  variables beside the shadcn set, no raw Tailwind color scales (`neutral-*`,
  `blue-*`, …), and no arbitrary hex / `rgb()` / `oklch()` colors in components.
- Rebrand by editing the existing token values in `src/styles.css`, not by
  inventing new token names or a second theme layer.
- Prefer `#/components/ui/*` primitives before hand-rolled controls that need
  their own color rules.

## Storybook

- Co-locate `*.stories.tsx` next to the component (`button.tsx` →
  `button.stories.tsx`). Titles: `UI/…`, `Shell/…`, `Feature/…`.
- Preview loads `src/styles.css` and a light/dark toolbar (`html.dark`). Verify
  both themes when changing tokens or variants.
- Story meaningful product states; mock callbacks with `fn()`. Do not put
  Clerk, server functions, or full routes in stories by default.
- Interaction examples live on `UI/Button` (`Clicked`, `Disabled` play
  functions). Run with `pnpm test:storybook`.
- Workflow: `docs/storybook-workflow.md`.
